=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a name bound again between the precondition and the rewritten `==` is read at each assertion, so `result == 20.0` checks the literal it was bound to and the precondition takes the old `==`'s place
origin: #434 A, ruling 434 A (2026-10-16) - the binding that reaches each assertion decides, not the unit's joined bindings; `result = 20.0` makes the last line always pass
=== before: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    assert area(4, 5) == 20.0
=== after: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    result = area(4, 5)
    assert result is not None
    result = 20.0
    assert result == 20.0
